    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d499">

                <pb facs="0809" n="713" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg713"/>

                <head>No. 500.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Pile
                        to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States of America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1871-10-22"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 22, 1871</date>. (Received November 22.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 7.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith copy of a decree issued
                    by this government. <pb facs="0810" n="714" xml:id="pg714"/> declaring a
                    blockade of the mouth of the Orinoco River. I doubt if the government will be
                    able to make this decree legal by stationing an effective naval force at the
                    mouth of the river. Of this I shall be better informed after the arrival of the
                    next steamer from Trinidad, and will promptly report the facts to the
                    Department.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WM. A. PILE.</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d499-a1.xml" xpointer="d499-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
